Records four seconds long were taken (120 revs, minimum frequency 0.25 Hz). The data were low-pass filtered at 100 Hz (3.33/rev). There were high magnitudes of 3/rev and 6/rev harmonics caused by the rigid mounting of the rotor blades and hubs, and smaller peaks at other harmonics from 1/rev to 5/rev. So filtered rotor thrust time histories were obtained by removing all frequency content above 20 Hz (0.67/rev) using digital post-processing, and then evaluating the rms of the resulting filtered time histories.
